        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Q9zlK",
          "name": "Rules",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$space-3",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "mjkA1",
              "name": "section head",
              "height": 17,
              "gap": 12,
              "alignItems": "center",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "dpdQK",
                  "name": "t Rules",
                  "fill": "$text",
                  "content": "Rules",
                  "lineHeight": 1.3,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-heading",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "zSkN4",
                  "name": "t numbered after the 16 of",
                  "fill": "$faint",
                  "content": "numbered after the 16 of `Editor components`; each names its token",
                  "lineHeight": 1.3,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "ifo7Z",
              "name": "rules",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": "$space-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "SiJb5",
                  "name": "rule 17.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "17. File-type tag: 3 characters right-aligned in a 24 px ($space-5) cell left of the name where a folder row's triangle sits, ending at the triangle cell's right edge, then the same 8 px gap a folder has, so a file's name and a folder's name at one level start on one x; at $type-body in its language's `$code-*` token over its glyphs alone, the second exception of `design/foundation.md` after the diff lines; a folder, a dotfile with no known type and an unknown extension carry no tag and keep the cells empty.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "G4mGkG",
                  "name": "rule 18.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "18. Indent guides: one 24 px ($space-5) cell per level above the row; under an open folder one vertical 1 px rule in $border at the cell's x + 6, under the centre of the folder's 12 px triangle cell (the glyph at x 3), from its first open child's top to its last one's bottom, the full height of every child row; no tick, no `tee`, no `end` elbow (the human's word of 2026-10-24, `corpus/08-tree-feedback.md`). A folder row is the triangle cell, 8 px ($space-2, one character of the body font as the scale rounds it) and the name, so the name of a row at depth d starts at 36 + 24·d (32 + 24·d on a phone, whose pad is 12). A file's tag cell ends at the triangle cell's right edge and reaches 12 px into the parent's cell, 6 px clear of its rail.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "lWKOz",
                  "name": "rule 19.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "19. Dimmed: an entry `git check-ignore` excludes (`.build`, `node_modules`, `dist`, `.env`) shows its triangle, tag and name in $faint and keeps its row, its badge and its click; its children dim too; the daemon says which listed paths are ignored.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "hZZK8",
                  "name": "rule 20.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "20. Compact row: a chain of folders that each hold exactly one folder and nothing else is one row named by the chain, `Web/terminal`; its triangle folds the whole chain and its badge is the last folder's; a file at any link ends the chain, so `Web/terminal/src` is not compacted.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "O8xfw",
                  "name": "rule 21.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "21. Keyboard selection: one row, a 1 px inset outline in $muted (a grey, never an owned colour), drawn while the tree has focus and following a click; the open file's row keeps $surface-2 and may be the selected one; `↑` `↓` move it, `←` folds an open folder or goes to the parent, `→` opens a closed folder or goes to its first child, `Enter` opens a file or toggles a folder, `Home` and `End` the first and last row.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "m1Kcs",
                  "name": "rule 22.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "22. Switcher: the project name in the header is a button, `kitterm ▼`, the name in $text and the triangle in $faint at $mark-size-disclosure; a tap opens the list under the header at the sidebar's content x (12 px, so no tab glyph peeks out beside it), 760 px wide, on $bg with a 1 px $border and a 2 px radius: `REGISTERED N` then `DISCOVERED N` in $faint weight 600, one home line per project with `[x]` on the current project in $text and `[ ]` on the others in $muted; a choice opens `/edit?path=<root>`, after the switch question while the buffer is edited; Esc or a tap outside closes it.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "K3efV",
                  "name": "rule 23.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "23. Home: `/edit` with no path, the header `Projects` with `open in terminal` (`/`); the same two labels, one line per project at $line-compact (44 px below 768): the name in $text in a 22ch cell, the root under `~` in $faint (the one cell that grows and truncates), the branch in $muted in 9ch (`–` for a root that is no checkout), `M N` at the right (`M` $warning weight 600, N in $muted; nothing when clean); the line opens `/edit?path=<root>`; a phone keeps the name, the branch and `M N`.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HF5ER",
                  "name": "rule 24.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "24. Empty home: `No project is registered and no pane sits in a checkout.  kitterm project add <path>`, the command in $text after two spaces, the sentence in $muted, as the fleet view's first-run notes.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Vzrre",
                  "name": "rule 25.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "25. Palette: ⌘P (Ctrl+P elsewhere) over a $scrim, a 640 px box 24 px under the header on $bg with a 1 px $border and a 2 px radius; the query line 44 px, the text in $text with a 1 px caret, the placeholder `file name or project` in $faint, the keys `↑ ↓ choose · Enter opens · Esc closes` in $faint at the right; `FILES N` then `PROJECTS N` labels; a file row is the tag cell, the name in $text with the matched letters at weight 600 underlined, the directory in $faint; a project row is the home line without the radio; the selected row on $surface-2; at most 8 file rows, then `N more files: type more of the name` in $faint; `No file or project matches.` when nothing does; the index is `git ls-files` for a checkout, the listing walk for a root that is none.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "jqeW9",
                  "name": "rule 26.",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "26. The terminal idiom holds: $mono, hairlines in $border, no radius above 2 px, no shadow, no transition, 44 px targets below 768; the owned colours paint a mark, a badge, the diff lines and a state's run of text, never a background, a border or a selection; a tag's colour is a kind, not a state.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
